1
00:00:33,346 --> 00:00:38,059
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

2
00:00:42,438 --> 00:00:44,399
‎LAUNDRY HUB

3
00:00:53,408 --> 00:00:54,242
‎What the heck?

4
00:00:59,747 --> 00:01:02,667
‎Don't move, or else we all die!

5
00:01:23,938 --> 00:01:24,939
‎Get down!

6
00:01:40,079 --> 00:01:41,080
‎Get in the cart.

7
00:02:02,185 --> 00:02:03,061
‎Watch out!

8
00:02:41,975 --> 00:02:42,892
‎Come in.

9
00:02:47,313 --> 00:02:48,648
‎So, what happened?

10
00:02:48,731 --> 00:02:49,565
‎Well…

11
00:02:50,149 --> 00:02:51,401
‎They got away.

12
00:02:57,031 --> 00:02:58,992
‎FINALE

13
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:06,416
‎Head to the stairs.

14
00:03:21,639 --> 00:03:22,640
‎Hold on.

15
00:03:23,266 --> 00:03:24,892
‎What are you doing here?

16
00:03:25,768 --> 00:03:28,438
‎Oh, you're here to save me.

17
00:03:29,188 --> 00:03:30,523
‎Hey, Park Gang Seong.

18
00:03:31,149 --> 00:03:34,152
‎Number 66 is on our side now.

19
00:03:34,235 --> 00:03:35,695
‎Put down your gun.

20
00:03:37,572 --> 00:03:40,116
‎I heard the person
‎who got my brother killed…

21
00:03:41,951 --> 00:03:43,119
‎was you.

22
00:03:43,745 --> 00:03:44,579
‎What…

23
00:03:45,747 --> 00:03:47,332
‎What are you talking about?

24
00:03:48,249 --> 00:03:51,002
‎I told you Park Yeong Gwang was killed

25
00:03:51,085 --> 00:03:52,587
‎by the South Korean bastards

26
00:03:52,670 --> 00:03:55,131
‎-during a mission--
‎-Didn't you say 66 killed him?

27
00:03:59,177 --> 00:04:00,928
‎No, what I meant was…

28
00:04:01,012 --> 00:04:02,221
‎Why are you so quiet?

29
00:04:04,098 --> 00:04:05,933
‎Go ahead and say it wasn't you.

30
00:04:09,187 --> 00:04:10,021
‎I…

31
00:04:12,357 --> 00:04:14,108
‎couldn't save your brother.

32
00:04:15,443 --> 00:04:16,486
‎That's it.

33
00:04:26,454 --> 00:04:27,372
‎Move.

34
00:04:28,873 --> 00:04:29,957
‎I said move!

35
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:33,252
‎You think doing this will keep you safe?

36
00:04:33,336 --> 00:04:36,047
‎You betrayed the Party's orders as well!

37
00:04:36,756 --> 00:04:39,967
‎I'll talk to the South Korean authorities.

38
00:04:40,051 --> 00:04:41,844
‎You and I can defect together

39
00:04:41,928 --> 00:04:43,471
‎-and find a way to live--
‎-Shut up!

40
00:04:47,975 --> 00:04:49,519
‎Let me ask you one thing.

41
00:04:52,522 --> 00:04:54,899
‎Why are you protecting that enemy bastard?

42
00:04:59,654 --> 00:05:00,488
‎Sang-a.

43
00:05:01,906 --> 00:05:02,740
‎It's okay.

44
00:05:18,005 --> 00:05:19,882
‎To protect my daughter.

45
00:05:26,097 --> 00:05:27,890
‎Protecting the people I care about…

46
00:05:29,434 --> 00:05:31,102
‎is more important…

47
00:05:33,813 --> 00:05:34,856
‎than killing my enemy.

48
00:05:44,782 --> 00:05:46,200
‎You'll get another chance.

49
00:05:48,035 --> 00:05:49,078
‎Trust me and walk away.

50
00:06:06,554 --> 00:06:07,763
‎Hurry up and get in!

51
00:06:10,850 --> 00:06:13,227
‎I was told to move the truck,
‎so I had to circle around.

52
00:06:14,687 --> 00:06:15,605
‎What's going on?

53
00:06:33,539 --> 00:06:34,373
‎Mr. Kim.

54
00:06:38,044 --> 00:06:39,587
‎Let it through.

55
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:40,963
‎SECURITY CHECK

56
00:06:44,467 --> 00:06:47,511
‎I heard gunshots, and it sounded serious.
‎Did something happen?

57
00:06:47,595 --> 00:06:49,931
‎No, it's nothing serious.
‎It's just an internal issue.

58
00:06:50,014 --> 00:06:52,516
‎-You can leave.
‎-But I have more laundry to pick up.

59
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,268
‎You can do it next time.
‎Please leave for now.

60
00:06:54,352 --> 00:06:55,228
‎We have an urgent situation.

61
00:06:55,311 --> 00:06:57,271
‎-Okay, then. Good night.
‎-Good night.

62
00:07:03,903 --> 00:07:04,946
‎Close the barricades.

63
00:07:22,296 --> 00:07:23,464
‎You can get out now.

64
00:07:26,842 --> 00:07:28,302
‎-Take him to a hospital.
‎-What?

65
00:07:28,386 --> 00:07:30,471
‎But a gunshot wound
‎is hard to keep under wraps.

66
00:07:30,555 --> 00:07:32,473
‎Contact General Jang. He'll help.

67
00:07:32,557 --> 00:07:34,475
‎What happened to Mr. Sung Han-soo
‎and Mr. Park Jin-cheol?

68
00:07:34,559 --> 00:07:37,436
‎I saw them
‎getting into Ju Gang-chan's car.

69
00:07:38,062 --> 00:07:39,522
‎-Ju Gang-chan?
‎-Yeah.

70
00:07:45,361 --> 00:07:46,320
‎Han-soo.

71
00:07:46,988 --> 00:07:48,114
‎Where are you?

72
00:07:48,948 --> 00:07:49,824
‎What's wrong?

73
00:07:50,616 --> 00:07:51,826
‎Kim, I'm sorry.

74
00:07:56,038 --> 00:07:56,872
‎Mr. Kim.

75
00:07:57,873 --> 00:07:58,708
‎Mr. Kim?

76
00:08:10,094 --> 00:08:10,970
‎Let's go.

77
00:08:31,616 --> 00:08:33,326
‎Are you really not going to tell us?

78
00:08:35,369 --> 00:08:36,495
‎Take him to a hospital.

79
00:08:37,288 --> 00:08:38,331
‎Okay.

80
00:08:58,392 --> 00:08:59,352
‎I'm sorry.

81
00:09:00,436 --> 00:09:01,395
‎If you don't come…

82
00:09:03,648 --> 00:09:04,774
‎the kids will die.

83
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:06,692
‎Please.

84
00:09:07,443 --> 00:09:08,277
‎I'm begging you.

85
00:09:10,112 --> 00:09:11,280
‎I'll be right there.

86
00:09:19,914 --> 00:09:21,791
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

87
00:09:21,874 --> 00:09:24,669
‎A FEW HOURS AGO

88
00:09:39,892 --> 00:09:40,851
‎Who are you?

89
00:09:42,770 --> 00:09:44,772
‎Damn it, I just mopped the floor.

90
00:09:46,607 --> 00:09:48,526
‎-It's him.
‎-This is a Taekwondo studio.

91
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:50,528
‎Take off your shoes first.

92
00:10:00,621 --> 00:10:04,125
‎-Whip it up, whip it up, up and down
‎-Whip it up

93
00:10:04,208 --> 00:10:06,752
‎-Whip it up, whip it up
‎-Whip it up

94
00:10:07,503 --> 00:10:08,671
‎Whip it…

95
00:10:10,089 --> 00:10:11,173
‎What the hell?

96
00:10:11,799 --> 00:10:13,175
‎Are you Da-bin?

97
00:10:13,259 --> 00:10:14,468
‎Yes, that's me.

98
00:10:14,552 --> 00:10:15,553
‎Who are you?

99
00:10:24,603 --> 00:10:25,438
‎Take him.

100
00:10:31,402 --> 00:10:32,611
‎Mister.

101
00:10:32,695 --> 00:10:34,572
‎Why are you doing this to us?

102
00:10:35,281 --> 00:10:37,700
‎Please let us go.

103
00:10:37,783 --> 00:10:39,910
‎Untie us right now!

104
00:10:39,994 --> 00:10:40,995
‎Mister,

105
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,289
‎please let us go.

106
00:10:44,832 --> 00:10:46,292
‎Please!

107
00:10:46,375 --> 00:10:47,877
‎JUHAK CONSTRUCTION CHAIRMAN JU GANG-CHAN

108
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,253
‎Ready, sir.

109
00:11:55,861 --> 00:11:58,614
‎So you're willing to risk your life
‎for your friends' kids.

110
00:12:01,283 --> 00:12:02,451
‎I have to say I'm surprised.

111
00:12:49,665 --> 00:12:52,126
‎Then again, you two did the same.

112
00:12:56,755 --> 00:12:58,173
‎Now you get to choose.

113
00:13:00,634 --> 00:13:02,261
‎Will you kill your friend…

114
00:13:06,056 --> 00:13:07,266
‎or will you kill your kids?

115
00:13:24,742 --> 00:13:26,660
‎I'm really sorry…

116
00:13:30,956 --> 00:13:32,124
‎for dragging you into this.

117
00:13:36,754 --> 00:13:38,839
‎If 66 dies, the kids will live.

118
00:13:38,922 --> 00:13:40,132
‎Do you really have a choice?

119
00:13:58,484 --> 00:13:59,860
‎-No!
‎-Da-bin!

120
00:13:59,943 --> 00:14:00,944
‎-Stop!
‎-Da-bin!

121
00:14:01,028 --> 00:14:02,321
‎-Dad!
‎-Father!

122
00:14:02,404 --> 00:14:03,989
‎Dad, please help!

123
00:14:04,823 --> 00:14:05,741
‎Father…

124
00:14:05,824 --> 00:14:08,661
‎I'll do whatever you want, so stop it!

125
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:10,579
‎Kim.

126
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:26,428
‎Jin-cheol.

127
00:14:27,513 --> 00:14:28,389
‎Han-soo.

128
00:14:30,724 --> 00:14:32,017
‎You have to take me down…

129
00:14:34,937 --> 00:14:35,854
‎for the kids to live.

130
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:57,584
‎Get it together!

131
00:15:05,843 --> 00:15:06,719
‎Get up.

132
00:15:10,222 --> 00:15:11,598
‎Kim!

133
00:15:12,599 --> 00:15:14,435
‎There must be a way.

134
00:15:18,272 --> 00:15:19,398
‎Focus on the kids.

135
00:15:20,899 --> 00:15:21,942
‎Focus!

136
00:15:38,959 --> 00:15:40,377
‎Han-soo!

137
00:16:05,319 --> 00:16:06,278
‎Kim.

138
00:16:26,006 --> 00:16:27,883
‎This is a bit of a letdown.

139
00:16:30,385 --> 00:16:32,429
‎You're not taking this seriously.

140
00:16:41,522 --> 00:16:42,898
‎I'll give you five minutes.

141
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:45,109
‎If you don't kill him by then,

142
00:16:45,984 --> 00:16:47,820
‎I'll shoot the kids myself.

143
00:16:52,866 --> 00:16:54,368
‎Father!

144
00:16:54,451 --> 00:16:56,203
‎-Dad!
‎-Then I'll shoot 66.

145
00:16:56,286 --> 00:16:58,247
‎Please help!

146
00:16:58,330 --> 00:16:59,331
‎Father.

147
00:16:59,414 --> 00:17:01,583
‎-Dad!
‎-Father!

148
00:17:01,667 --> 00:17:03,377
‎-Father!
‎-Dad!

149
00:17:04,253 --> 00:17:05,170
‎Father…

150
00:17:07,297 --> 00:17:08,465
‎What are you waiting for?

151
00:17:11,802 --> 00:17:13,345
‎Your kids are calling for you.

152
00:17:17,224 --> 00:17:18,684
‎Dad!

153
00:17:18,767 --> 00:17:19,685
‎Dad!

154
00:17:21,145 --> 00:17:22,187
‎Dad!

155
00:17:26,608 --> 00:17:29,111
‎-Father!
‎-Dad!

156
00:17:49,423 --> 00:17:52,217
‎More, more, more!

157
00:18:02,811 --> 00:18:03,687
‎Get up.

158
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:05,981
‎Get up! I said get up!

159
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:17,618
‎Get up!

160
00:18:17,701 --> 00:18:19,161
‎Get up!

161
00:19:05,249 --> 00:19:06,333
‎Tae-hun…

162
00:19:08,210 --> 00:19:09,086
‎and Da-bin…

163
00:19:14,216 --> 00:19:15,300
‎You have to save them.

164
00:19:18,929 --> 00:19:19,805
‎And…

165
00:19:25,769 --> 00:19:26,812
‎please take care…

166
00:19:29,147 --> 00:19:30,190
‎of Min-ji.

167
00:19:45,664 --> 00:19:47,582
‎How sad,
‎you're going to miss Min-ji so much.

168
00:19:53,046 --> 00:19:54,006
‎Come back.

169
00:19:56,258 --> 00:19:57,342
‎I'll wait for you.

170
00:20:00,012 --> 00:20:01,305
‎You'll come back.

171
00:20:02,306 --> 00:20:03,515
‎You're my dad.

172
00:20:38,050 --> 00:20:38,925
‎One.

173
00:20:41,386 --> 00:20:42,346
‎Two.

174
00:20:45,015 --> 00:20:45,849
‎Three.

175
00:20:48,018 --> 00:20:49,519
‎-Dad!
‎-Uncle!

176
00:20:59,196 --> 00:21:00,030
‎Four.

177
00:21:01,406 --> 00:21:02,949
‎-Damn it.
‎-Get up.

178
00:21:03,033 --> 00:21:05,285
‎Get up! I said get up!

179
00:21:05,994 --> 00:21:06,953
‎Three seconds.

180
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:13,251
‎Three seconds is enough.

181
00:21:29,351 --> 00:21:31,144
‎-Da-bin!
‎-Dad!

182
00:21:31,228 --> 00:21:33,313
‎-Da-bin!
‎-Dad!

183
00:21:34,064 --> 00:21:36,358
‎Dad, you got shot. Are you okay?

184
00:21:36,441 --> 00:21:38,860
‎-I'm okay. I didn't get shot.
‎-Are you okay?

185
00:21:38,944 --> 00:21:40,320
‎I'm fine.

186
00:21:40,404 --> 00:21:42,906
‎-I dodged it.
‎-Oh, you did?

187
00:21:42,989 --> 00:21:45,033
‎-You didn't get shot?
‎-No, I didn't.

188
00:21:45,117 --> 00:21:47,202
‎Are you okay? You must've been so scared.

189
00:21:47,285 --> 00:21:49,538
‎-My poor Da-bin!
‎-Dad, I'm fine.

190
00:21:49,621 --> 00:21:52,874
‎-If anything had happened to you…
‎-I said I'm fine!

191
00:21:52,958 --> 00:21:54,167
‎Hurry up and free me.

192
00:21:54,251 --> 00:21:56,002
‎Jeez, this is so annoying.

193
00:21:56,086 --> 00:21:57,879
‎-That hurts!
‎-Stop touching my hair!

194
00:21:57,963 --> 00:21:59,131
‎I won't touch your hair.

195
00:22:00,841 --> 00:22:02,592
‎You're okay, you're okay.

196
00:22:02,676 --> 00:22:04,177
‎Yeah, I'm fine.

197
00:22:04,261 --> 00:22:05,095
‎Let's go.

198
00:22:06,930 --> 00:22:07,889
‎Are you okay?

199
00:22:07,973 --> 00:22:09,975
‎-I'm fine.
‎-Can you get up?

200
00:22:13,228 --> 00:22:14,062
‎I'm okay.

201
00:22:15,856 --> 00:22:16,690
‎I'm fine.

202
00:22:23,989 --> 00:22:25,282
‎Kim!

203
00:22:30,370 --> 00:22:31,329
‎You okay?

204
00:22:32,122 --> 00:22:33,456
‎What about the kids?

205
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:35,292
‎-They're fine.
‎-Are you okay?

206
00:22:35,375 --> 00:22:36,293
‎What do you think?

207
00:22:36,376 --> 00:22:37,502
‎Of course, he's not okay.

208
00:22:37,586 --> 00:22:39,462
‎Right, you got beaten up by us, after all.

209
00:22:39,546 --> 00:22:40,714
‎It took four seconds.

210
00:22:40,797 --> 00:22:42,382
‎That's why he got shot.

211
00:22:42,465 --> 00:22:44,217
‎It just grazed me.

212
00:22:44,301 --> 00:22:46,052
‎-You okay?
‎-What do you think?

213
00:22:46,136 --> 00:22:47,554
‎Of course, he's not okay.

214
00:22:51,975 --> 00:22:53,059
‎He seems okay.

215
00:22:56,605 --> 00:22:57,647
‎Hey, chairman.

216
00:22:59,191 --> 00:23:01,318
‎We have some unfinished business.

217
00:23:03,445 --> 00:23:04,779
‎A parent meeting.

218
00:23:14,706 --> 00:23:16,833
‎What else is there to do?

219
00:23:17,542 --> 00:23:18,752
‎I have to keep my promise.

220
00:23:20,295 --> 00:23:21,880
‎Are you okay to drive?

221
00:23:21,963 --> 00:23:23,381
‎I guess he is.

222
00:23:40,232 --> 00:23:41,733
‎What about the kids?

223
00:23:41,816 --> 00:23:44,361
‎Shouldn't we keep an eye on them
‎so they don't go out?

224
00:23:44,444 --> 00:23:45,862
‎Does Tae-hun ever listen to you?

225
00:23:45,946 --> 00:23:47,364
‎Of course, he doesn't.

226
00:23:47,447 --> 00:23:50,325
‎He even attacks his own father.

227
00:23:51,910 --> 00:23:54,955
‎At least Da-bin doesn't attack me.

228
00:23:55,038 --> 00:23:56,206
‎She just ignores me.

229
00:23:58,041 --> 00:23:59,960
‎We should leave them with someone
‎who can intimidate them.

230
00:24:00,877 --> 00:24:02,379
‎-Like who?
‎-I know someone.

231
00:24:02,462 --> 00:24:03,880
‎Someone scarier than me.

232
00:24:03,964 --> 00:24:07,842
‎Actually, they might be
‎the scariest person on the planet.

233
00:24:09,427 --> 00:24:10,262
‎Let's go.

234
00:24:14,224 --> 00:24:15,225
‎Man, my legs.

235
00:24:16,393 --> 00:24:17,435
‎My poor legs.

236
00:24:18,812 --> 00:24:20,230
‎My legs are killing me.

237
00:24:23,441 --> 00:24:24,609
‎My steering wheel!

238
00:24:26,736 --> 00:24:28,196
‎Come on!

239
00:24:32,075 --> 00:24:34,494
‎SECURITY COMMANDER KANG JI-YEONG

240
00:24:39,416 --> 00:24:40,667
‎Is this a joke?

241
00:24:40,750 --> 00:24:43,420
‎17TH AMPHIBIOUS MOBILE BRIGADE
‎RED DRAGON UNIT SPECIAL SECURITY BATTALION

242
00:24:44,004 --> 00:24:44,838
‎Honey…

243
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:49,301
‎Would you mind
‎watching the kids for a bit?

244
00:24:50,135 --> 00:24:52,846
‎If you could keep them in a room

245
00:24:52,929 --> 00:24:54,431
‎and protect them for a few days…

246
00:24:56,308 --> 00:24:58,393
‎Please?

247
00:24:59,394 --> 00:25:00,437
‎Please?

248
00:25:04,232 --> 00:25:06,776
‎This isn't a daycare center.

249
00:25:08,069 --> 00:25:08,945
‎You little punk!

250
00:25:10,697 --> 00:25:12,991
‎This is fake. Do you have any guns, lady?

251
00:25:13,074 --> 00:25:15,327
‎I told you not to call me that.

252
00:25:15,827 --> 00:25:16,995
‎Be quiet and go away.

253
00:25:19,456 --> 00:25:20,749
‎Mom, lend me your phone.

254
00:25:21,374 --> 00:25:22,375
‎Da-bin, be quiet.

255
00:25:25,337 --> 00:25:27,547
‎I told you not to get into trouble.

256
00:25:27,630 --> 00:25:28,923
‎I didn't get into trouble.

257
00:25:29,007 --> 00:25:31,176
‎I just felt so bad for Kim
‎that I had no choice but to help.

258
00:25:31,259 --> 00:25:33,803
‎I had no choice
‎because Jin-cheol told me to help.

259
00:25:34,596 --> 00:25:36,556
‎Kim? Again?

260
00:25:36,639 --> 00:25:38,183
‎I ought to just…

261
00:25:38,266 --> 00:25:39,142
‎That's not true.

262
00:25:41,811 --> 00:25:42,854
‎It's not true, honey.

263
00:25:44,189 --> 00:25:45,565
‎I wanted to help him.

264
00:25:46,483 --> 00:25:47,317
‎It was my choice.

265
00:25:48,360 --> 00:25:49,235
‎My friend…

266
00:25:50,695 --> 00:25:53,490
‎had to do one last mission
‎to see his daughter again.

267
00:25:55,325 --> 00:25:56,534
‎So I wanted to help him.

268
00:25:58,578 --> 00:25:59,412
‎Me too.

269
00:26:11,174 --> 00:26:14,052
‎Still, you shouldn't have
‎put the kids in danger.

270
00:26:15,845 --> 00:26:16,679
‎I'm sorry, honey.

271
00:26:16,763 --> 00:26:18,390
‎I'm sorry too.

272
00:26:22,435 --> 00:26:23,770
‎The kids will stay with me.

273
00:26:25,063 --> 00:26:26,606
‎I can't trust you two.

274
00:26:26,689 --> 00:26:27,899
‎-Honey!
‎-Honey!

275
00:26:27,982 --> 00:26:28,817
‎I mean, Ji-yeong.

276
00:26:30,276 --> 00:26:33,446
‎When will you middle-aged men grow up?

277
00:26:33,530 --> 00:26:35,573
‎Seriously, when will you…

278
00:26:36,408 --> 00:26:37,242
‎When…

279
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:39,494
‎Honey.

280
00:26:39,577 --> 00:26:41,788
‎Have I told you

281
00:26:41,871 --> 00:26:42,872
‎-that I love--
‎-Get out.

282
00:26:42,956 --> 00:26:43,873
‎-Yes, he has.
‎-Let's go.

283
00:26:43,957 --> 00:26:45,208
‎-Hurry.
‎-Sit properly.

284
00:26:45,959 --> 00:26:48,169
‎Eat as much as you can in one sitting,
‎and don't ask for snacks.

285
00:26:48,253 --> 00:26:49,879
‎-You know what to do, right?
‎-What?

286
00:26:49,963 --> 00:26:52,006
‎And don't ask
‎for the Wi-Fi password, okay?

287
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:54,175
‎-Why?
‎-Don't ask. Just be quiet.

288
00:26:54,259 --> 00:26:56,094
‎-Got it?
‎-Yeah, just go already.

289
00:26:56,177 --> 00:26:57,720
‎-Don't make her mad.
‎-Okay, okay.

290
00:26:57,804 --> 00:26:59,097
‎All right, attention!

291
00:26:59,180 --> 00:27:00,014
‎Salute!

292
00:27:01,599 --> 00:27:02,434
‎Hands down.

293
00:27:04,018 --> 00:27:04,853
‎Dad.

294
00:27:04,936 --> 00:27:05,812
‎Do as she says.

295
00:27:12,026 --> 00:27:12,944
‎Are you hungry?

296
00:27:15,238 --> 00:27:16,072
‎Yes, I am.

297
00:27:16,698 --> 00:27:19,242
‎Those guys didn't even feed you?

298
00:27:19,325 --> 00:27:21,786
‎What do you want?
‎Want me to order ‎jjajangmyeon‎?

299
00:27:24,873 --> 00:27:31,713
‎INTER-KOREAN GOVERNMENT TALKS

300
00:27:35,049 --> 00:27:38,094
‎I'm pleased that both sides
‎could come to an agreement.

301
00:27:38,678 --> 00:27:40,388
‎I hope that the North and the South

302
00:27:40,472 --> 00:27:43,308
‎can move toward a cooperative future
‎through the free-trade zone.

303
00:27:43,391 --> 00:27:44,225
‎Likewise.

304
00:27:46,227 --> 00:27:48,021
‎Thank you, everyone.

305
00:27:49,522 --> 00:27:52,025
‎Can the two of you please shake hands?

306
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:03,912
‎I think we have other matters to discuss.

307
00:28:05,121 --> 00:28:06,873
‎About what happened last night, that is.

308
00:28:21,387 --> 00:28:22,555
‎As you know,

309
00:28:23,264 --> 00:28:27,852
‎we've done our best to accommodate
‎the North's requests during this visit.

310
00:28:28,811 --> 00:28:29,646
‎Don't you agree?

311
00:28:29,729 --> 00:28:33,566
‎It was all for the good
‎of inter-Korean cooperation.

312
00:28:34,234 --> 00:28:37,028
‎What are your thoughts, sir?

313
00:28:39,572 --> 00:28:40,490
‎But you know,

314
00:28:41,741 --> 00:28:46,204
‎I think what happened last night
‎was out of line.

315
00:28:46,287 --> 00:28:47,789
‎Shouldn't you take responsibility

316
00:28:48,623 --> 00:28:52,627
‎for causing such a scene
‎on South Korean soil?

317
00:28:52,710 --> 00:28:53,878
‎That was…

318
00:28:57,215 --> 00:28:58,675
‎There was an internal issue.

319
00:28:58,758 --> 00:28:59,926
‎And that issue

320
00:29:00,009 --> 00:29:02,428
‎almost turned South Korea
‎into a battlefield.

321
00:29:02,512 --> 00:29:04,514
‎No, we had no intention of--

322
00:29:04,597 --> 00:29:05,723
‎Now, now.

323
00:29:10,061 --> 00:29:12,021
‎Considering the outcome of these talks,

324
00:29:12,939 --> 00:29:18,862
‎we won't take official retaliatory action
‎against the North.

325
00:29:19,612 --> 00:29:20,780
‎However,

326
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:23,741
‎let's settle this with the understanding

327
00:29:24,701 --> 00:29:27,996
‎that we have zero responsibility
‎for the casualties on your side.

328
00:29:32,959 --> 00:29:33,877
‎Understood.

329
00:29:34,544 --> 00:29:39,591
‎WE WELCOME THE NORTH KOREAN DELEGATION
‎TO JUHAK HERITAGE RESORT

330
00:29:55,773 --> 00:29:56,941
‎Listen carefully.

331
00:29:58,026 --> 00:30:01,821
‎The Party will be told that Ri Eung Ryeong
‎and 66 have been summarily executed.

332
00:30:02,864 --> 00:30:06,993
‎If word gets out that we lost them
‎after the South handed them over to us,

333
00:30:07,076 --> 00:30:10,705
‎we're all going to have to
‎take responsibility.

334
00:30:12,707 --> 00:30:14,918
‎I've already spoken
‎with the delegation officials,

335
00:30:15,627 --> 00:30:17,295
‎so make sure to keep your men quiet.

336
00:30:17,921 --> 00:30:18,755
‎Understand?

337
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:20,381
‎Yes, sir.

338
00:30:29,849 --> 00:30:31,768
‎-What are you talking about?
‎-Over there.

339
00:30:32,518 --> 00:30:34,437
‎That's a person, right?

340
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:35,438
‎-What the heck?
‎-What is that?

341
00:30:35,521 --> 00:30:37,065
‎That's a person, for crying out loud!

342
00:30:37,148 --> 00:30:39,859
‎-Contact EMS and call for backup.
‎-Yes, sir.

343
00:30:39,943 --> 00:30:41,694
‎-Sir, stay right here.
‎-Okay.

344
00:30:41,778 --> 00:30:44,072
‎MYEONGJIN CENTRAL HOSPITAL

345
00:30:47,325 --> 00:30:48,785
‎VIP1
‎UNIDENTIFIED PERSON

346
00:31:28,616 --> 00:31:30,994
‎Goodness, Director General.

347
00:31:32,203 --> 00:31:33,413
‎How do you feel?

348
00:31:33,997 --> 00:31:34,914
‎I'm fine.

349
00:31:45,883 --> 00:31:47,051
‎Start recording.

350
00:31:50,513 --> 00:31:51,597
‎What's the rush?

351
00:31:53,307 --> 00:31:54,600
‎Quickly, quickly.

352
00:31:54,684 --> 00:31:56,144
‎This is how it is in the South.

353
00:31:56,227 --> 00:31:57,395
‎You should get used to it too.

354
00:31:58,771 --> 00:32:00,523
‎All right, then.

355
00:32:00,606 --> 00:32:03,151
‎Let's start with the status of the ICBMs.

356
00:32:05,653 --> 00:32:08,114
‎I have one last condition.

357
00:32:09,615 --> 00:32:10,450
‎A condition?

358
00:32:12,952 --> 00:32:16,164
‎After I give you all the information,

359
00:32:16,748 --> 00:32:20,585
‎send me to Macau for asylum.

360
00:32:24,547 --> 00:32:25,798
‎I'll think about it

361
00:32:26,382 --> 00:32:28,176
‎depending on the quality
‎of the information.

362
00:32:30,928 --> 00:32:34,390
‎So our understanding
‎is that the Strategic Rocket Force

363
00:32:34,474 --> 00:32:36,267
‎is structured around a three-axis system.

364
00:32:36,350 --> 00:32:38,603
‎Cholsan County, North Pyongan Province.

365
00:32:38,686 --> 00:32:40,396
‎Chonchon County, Chagang Province.

366
00:32:40,480 --> 00:32:43,191
‎And Kilju County, North Hamgyong Province.

367
00:32:43,274 --> 00:32:48,279
‎At least 12 transporter erector launchers
‎are currently in service.

368
00:32:49,322 --> 00:32:51,657
‎What about the current range?

369
00:32:51,741 --> 00:32:53,576
‎Not only can they easily reach Guam,

370
00:32:54,535 --> 00:32:56,621
‎but Alaska

371
00:32:56,704 --> 00:33:00,583
‎and the US West Coast
‎are also within striking range.

372
00:33:01,667 --> 00:33:05,546
‎How are they handling the fuel transition?

373
00:33:05,630 --> 00:33:07,965
‎It's liquid-based right now,

374
00:33:08,049 --> 00:33:13,262
‎but they're currently transitioning over
‎to solid fuel.

375
00:33:14,305 --> 00:33:16,891
‎That's why I'm needed.

376
00:33:16,974 --> 00:33:19,519
‎You see, all the information

377
00:33:20,103 --> 00:33:21,604
‎is right in here.

378
00:33:52,426 --> 00:33:57,390
‎VIP1
‎UNIDENTIFIED PERSON

379
00:35:13,633 --> 00:35:18,846
‎PATIENT TRANSPORT

380
00:35:27,104 --> 00:35:28,773
‎You kept your promise.

381
00:35:29,523 --> 00:35:30,733
‎What are you going to do?

382
00:35:32,652 --> 00:35:33,736
‎I'll take it from here.

383
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:37,281
‎It'd be a shame
‎to finish off an enemy so easily.

384
00:36:01,764 --> 00:36:04,141
‎I need you to do one last thing for me.

385
00:36:04,225 --> 00:36:05,726
‎No matter what happens,

386
00:36:05,810 --> 00:36:08,521
‎promise me you'll survive.

387
00:36:13,150 --> 00:36:13,985
‎What are you doing?

388
00:36:15,903 --> 00:36:17,029
‎If you're done, go.

389
00:36:27,331 --> 00:36:28,291
‎I wish you and your daughter…

390
00:36:30,668 --> 00:36:31,544
‎a good life.

391
00:36:36,841 --> 00:36:38,009
‎I'll stay alive too.

392
00:36:41,095 --> 00:36:41,929
‎Good.

393
00:36:43,222 --> 00:36:44,056
‎Stay alive…

394
00:36:47,059 --> 00:36:48,144
‎no matter what.

395
00:37:11,834 --> 00:37:13,252
‎COMMANDER'S OFFICE
‎CHEONSAN UNIT

396
00:37:13,961 --> 00:37:14,795
‎So?

397
00:37:15,421 --> 00:37:17,757
‎Who kidnapped Ri Eung Ryeong?

398
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:20,301
‎We have yet to identify the suspect, sir.

399
00:37:20,926 --> 00:37:22,303
‎We're currently analyzing CCTV footage,

400
00:37:22,887 --> 00:37:24,722
‎and we'll mobilize a team
‎once we track their movements.

401
00:37:24,805 --> 00:37:26,807
‎Forget it. Let it go.

402
00:37:27,350 --> 00:37:28,184
‎Sir?

403
00:37:28,267 --> 00:37:30,811
‎We got all the information
‎we needed out of him.

404
00:37:31,604 --> 00:37:35,066
‎It'd be a waste of taxpayer money
‎to keep him around longer.

405
00:37:36,525 --> 00:37:37,401
‎It doesn't matter

406
00:37:37,485 --> 00:37:39,987
‎whether he smuggles himself
‎out of the country or drops dead.

407
00:37:40,613 --> 00:37:42,782
‎Either way, it's for the better.

408
00:37:43,407 --> 00:37:44,450
‎But still…

409
00:37:44,533 --> 00:37:45,701
‎Just do as I say.

410
00:37:46,869 --> 00:37:47,787
‎That's an order.

411
00:38:32,123 --> 00:38:33,082
‎Is this Macau?

412
00:38:47,138 --> 00:38:48,055
‎Shit.

413
00:39:06,907 --> 00:39:07,825
‎THE SEAS OF OUR HOMELAND
‎DO NOT TOLERATE LIES

414
00:39:07,908 --> 00:39:08,868
‎THE COASTLINE IS THE FRONT LINE
‎OF NATIONAL DEFENSE!

415
00:39:10,703 --> 00:39:12,121
‎No, it can't be.

416
00:39:15,291 --> 00:39:16,375
‎F****** hell!

417
00:39:16,459 --> 00:39:17,710
‎Don't move!

418
00:39:17,793 --> 00:39:19,253
‎Stay right there!

419
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:22,798
‎-Stop!
‎-Stop right there!

420
00:39:24,049 --> 00:39:25,092
‎Stop!

421
00:39:26,927 --> 00:39:28,220
‎Stop right there!

422
00:39:37,354 --> 00:39:42,401
‎JUHAK CONSTRUCTION CO., LTD.

423
00:39:42,985 --> 00:39:44,445
‎CHO PYEONG-GYEON

424
00:40:03,797 --> 00:40:04,632
‎It's me, sir.

425
00:40:04,715 --> 00:40:05,674
‎Hey.

426
00:40:06,258 --> 00:40:08,761
‎My goodness. Are you alive and well?

427
00:40:08,844 --> 00:40:12,097
‎What made you call me all of a sudden?

428
00:40:12,181 --> 00:40:14,183
‎I called to ask you a favor.

429
00:40:14,934 --> 00:40:15,768
‎A favor?

430
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:17,520
‎What is it?

431
00:40:19,104 --> 00:40:20,064
‎I need you to dissolve

432
00:40:20,898 --> 00:40:22,483
‎Juhak Construction.

433
00:40:23,150 --> 00:40:24,193
‎Goodness.

434
00:40:24,276 --> 00:40:26,362
‎You haven't called in over a decade,

435
00:40:26,445 --> 00:40:28,113
‎and that's what you ask me for?

436
00:40:28,697 --> 00:40:30,282
‎It has to do with my daughter.

437
00:40:30,908 --> 00:40:32,034
‎Please, sir.

438
00:40:32,117 --> 00:40:35,162
‎My goodness, that poor thing.

439
00:40:35,246 --> 00:40:36,205
‎Good heavens.

440
00:40:36,288 --> 00:40:38,332
‎She must be really big now.

441
00:40:38,916 --> 00:40:40,543
‎She's pretty like her mom, right?

442
00:40:41,210 --> 00:40:43,087
‎I understand.

443
00:40:43,170 --> 00:40:45,464
‎I've known her since she was born, so…

444
00:40:47,341 --> 00:40:49,009
‎Juhak Construction, huh?

445
00:40:50,803 --> 00:40:51,679
‎All right.

446
00:40:52,304 --> 00:40:53,347
‎You got it.

447
00:40:55,224 --> 00:40:56,183
‎Thank you.

448
00:40:56,267 --> 00:40:58,519
‎Just wait a few days.

449
00:40:59,103 --> 00:41:00,813
‎Juhak Construction is nothing.

450
00:41:00,896 --> 00:41:04,149
‎I'll chop it up like a cucumber

451
00:41:04,233 --> 00:41:06,360
‎and make a salad out of it.

452
00:41:07,027 --> 00:41:09,029
‎You know this will cost you, right?

453
00:41:09,572 --> 00:41:14,326
‎We're close, but we're professionals,
‎so I won't lower my fees.

454
00:41:14,994 --> 00:41:16,203
‎You understand, right?

455
00:41:16,287 --> 00:41:17,997
‎-Yes, I do.
‎-Good.

456
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:19,248
‎All right, then.

457
00:41:19,331 --> 00:41:20,583
‎I'll call you back.

458
00:41:21,375 --> 00:41:22,585
‎Thank you, sir.

459
00:41:36,348 --> 00:41:38,601
‎Prosecutors have conducted
‎a surprise search and seizure

460
00:41:38,684 --> 00:41:43,188
‎at Juhak Construction headquarters
‎and its affiliates earlier this morning.

461
00:41:43,272 --> 00:41:44,773
‎-What's your business here?
‎-The investigation team

462
00:41:44,857 --> 00:41:47,526
‎-We have a search and seizure warrant.
‎-is looking into suspicious cash flows

463
00:41:47,610 --> 00:41:51,405
‎of tens of billions of won
‎between Juhak Construction affiliates

464
00:41:51,488 --> 00:41:52,698
‎and political figures.

465
00:41:53,324 --> 00:41:56,243
‎The said team believes the repeated,
‎large-scale fund transfers

466
00:41:56,327 --> 00:41:59,580
‎were not legitimate business transactions

467
00:41:59,663 --> 00:42:02,666
‎and is now tracing their source
‎and where they were ultimately used.

468
00:42:03,834 --> 00:42:07,254
‎This investigation
‎was reportedly triggered

469
00:42:07,338 --> 00:42:09,465
‎after the Financial Intelligence Unit

470
00:42:09,548 --> 00:42:12,676
‎filed suspicious transaction reports
‎with the prosecution late last year.

471
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:14,470
‎Do you acknowledge the bribery charges?

472
00:42:14,553 --> 00:42:16,263
‎Are the claims of redevelopment bias true?

473
00:42:16,347 --> 00:42:17,973
‎-Please answer, Assemblyman!
‎-Let me pass.

474
00:42:18,057 --> 00:42:19,642
‎-Please comment!
‎-We can do this another time.

475
00:42:43,207 --> 00:42:44,958
‎Are you going on a trip abroad

476
00:42:45,459 --> 00:42:47,294
‎after selling out your country?

477
00:42:49,505 --> 00:42:50,923
‎-Arrest him.
‎-Yes, sir.

478
00:42:54,551 --> 00:42:55,969
‎Let go of me!

479
00:42:56,595 --> 00:42:57,429
‎Let go!

480
00:43:01,850 --> 00:43:03,143
‎CAMBODIA

481
00:43:03,227 --> 00:43:05,437
‎A court has issued an arrest warrant

482
00:43:05,521 --> 00:43:08,607
‎for Chairman Ju Gang-chan
‎of Juhak Construction

483
00:43:08,691 --> 00:43:11,193
‎on charges of kidnapping, murder,
‎and threatening national security.

484
00:43:11,276 --> 00:43:13,278
‎The court cited the severity of the crimes

485
00:43:13,362 --> 00:43:16,115
‎and the risk of evidence tampering
‎for its decision.

486
00:43:16,198 --> 00:43:19,827
‎Chairman Ju
‎is reportedly hospitalized in Seoul.

487
00:43:19,910 --> 00:43:21,620
‎Meanwhile, the prosecution has stated

488
00:43:21,704 --> 00:43:23,455
‎it'll expand the investigation to include

489
00:43:23,539 --> 00:43:26,166
‎the company's founding history
‎and the chairman's illegal activities.

490
00:43:28,627 --> 00:43:30,421
‎Hye-ri, I know what you did.

491
00:43:30,504 --> 00:43:31,338
‎Do you know Kim Min-ji?

492
00:43:31,422 --> 00:43:33,173
‎Dang, the police came by the school.

493
00:43:33,257 --> 00:43:35,217
‎-I heard his daughter left the country.
‎-Daughter of a murderer.

494
00:43:35,300 --> 00:43:37,136
‎-Interpol is after you too.
‎-She's going to prison with her dad.

495
00:43:37,219 --> 00:43:38,262
‎Ju Hye-ri is screwed.

496
00:43:51,900 --> 00:43:52,776
‎He's coming out!

497
00:43:55,529 --> 00:43:57,448
‎When did you start making contact
‎with North Korea?

498
00:43:57,531 --> 00:43:59,199
‎Are the murder allegations true?

499
00:43:59,283 --> 00:44:02,244
‎Are you aware that your daughter,
‎who fled abroad, has been arrested?

500
00:44:04,204 --> 00:44:05,831
‎-Please say something!
‎-A comment, please!

501
00:44:05,914 --> 00:44:07,082
‎Say something, asshole.

502
00:44:12,588 --> 00:44:13,422
‎How've you been?

503
00:44:25,684 --> 00:44:27,519
‎How does it feel
‎to get taken down by a dog?

504
00:44:28,479 --> 00:44:31,899
‎You pulled out my teeth,
‎but I still have my claws, you bastard!

505
00:44:47,164 --> 00:44:50,125
‎You should've returned
‎as soon as the mission was over.

506
00:44:51,335 --> 00:44:53,086
‎Where have you been

507
00:44:54,379 --> 00:44:55,631
‎looking like that?

508
00:44:58,634 --> 00:45:00,719
‎Didn't you miss your daughter?

509
00:45:03,555 --> 00:45:07,142
‎I had some business to take care of
‎for Min-ji's sake.

510
00:45:09,269 --> 00:45:10,103
‎So?

511
00:45:10,729 --> 00:45:11,980
‎Is the business taken care of?

512
00:45:15,400 --> 00:45:16,235
‎Yes.

513
00:45:18,403 --> 00:45:20,739
‎It's all over now.

514
00:45:22,574 --> 00:45:25,244
‎Then it's time for me
‎to wrap things up as well.

515
00:45:26,203 --> 00:45:27,246
‎Number 66…

516
00:45:30,415 --> 00:45:31,416
‎must die.

517
00:45:37,297 --> 00:45:41,176
‎The body of a man with a gunshot wound
‎was discovered by an herb collector

518
00:45:41,260 --> 00:45:43,428
‎in the woods near the resort

519
00:45:43,512 --> 00:45:45,973
‎where the North Korean delegation
‎was staying.

520
00:45:46,056 --> 00:45:49,142
‎The deceased has been identified
‎as a man in his forties, surnamed Kim,

521
00:45:49,226 --> 00:45:53,605
‎and police have launched an investigation
‎into the exact circumstances of his death.

522
00:45:55,899 --> 00:45:57,818
‎BODY WITH GUNSHOT WOUND DISCOVERED
‎NEAR NORTH KOREAN DELEGATION LODGING

523
00:45:59,444 --> 00:46:00,946
‎DECEASED IDENTIFIED AS MAN IN HIS FORTIES
‎INVESTIGATION UNDERWAY

524
00:46:20,007 --> 00:46:21,216
‎HIGH-PROFILE WANTED FUGITIVE
‎COMPREHENSIVE PROFILE

525
00:46:21,300 --> 00:46:22,968
‎YOUNGER YEARS
‎ESTIMATED CURRENT APPEARANCE

526
00:46:24,011 --> 00:46:25,887
‎DELETE THIS PROFILE?
‎NO / YES

527
00:46:52,122 --> 00:46:53,498
‎THE LATE KIM, THE LATE IM YU-JIN

528
00:47:46,927 --> 00:47:47,928
‎I'm back.

529
00:47:53,392 --> 00:47:55,977
‎I'm not going to run into your arms.

530
00:47:57,062 --> 00:47:58,230
‎That'd be too cheesy.

531
00:48:01,566 --> 00:48:02,567
‎You knew?

532
00:48:03,151 --> 00:48:04,820
‎Sang-a told me.

533
00:48:06,363 --> 00:48:07,864
‎She said you died.

534
00:48:09,950 --> 00:48:11,743
‎But that you'd come back alive.

535
00:48:26,383 --> 00:48:27,300
‎I promise

536
00:48:28,844 --> 00:48:30,178
‎never to leave you again.

537
00:48:32,681 --> 00:48:33,515
‎I'll always…

538
00:48:35,434 --> 00:48:37,769
‎be right by your side.

539
00:48:44,609 --> 00:48:45,485
‎Dad…

540
00:48:48,155 --> 00:48:50,657
‎Do you know how worried I was?

541
00:48:51,700 --> 00:48:54,536
‎I was so afraid
‎something had happened to you.

542
00:48:59,040 --> 00:49:01,251
‎Thank you for coming back.

543
00:49:13,305 --> 00:49:14,222
‎It's okay.

544
00:49:17,559 --> 00:49:19,269
‎Wow, the flowers are so pretty.

545
00:49:21,813 --> 00:49:23,523
‎I should come visit Mom more often.

546
00:49:25,734 --> 00:49:27,235
‎Did Mom like flowers too?

547
00:49:28,069 --> 00:49:28,904
‎Yeah.

548
00:49:30,489 --> 00:49:31,740
‎Maybe that's why I'm pretty.

549
00:49:32,365 --> 00:49:33,200
‎No.

550
00:49:33,909 --> 00:49:34,868
‎You're pretty

551
00:49:35,744 --> 00:49:37,162
‎because you take after your mom.

552
00:49:38,371 --> 00:49:39,206
‎You're right.

553
00:49:39,289 --> 00:49:41,082
‎I definitely don't get my looks from you.

554
00:49:41,708 --> 00:49:42,542
‎Jeez.

555
00:49:44,044 --> 00:49:45,754
‎What happens to us now?

556
00:49:48,089 --> 00:49:49,216
‎From now on,

557
00:49:50,175 --> 00:49:52,344
‎we're going to live completely new lives.

558
00:49:53,136 --> 00:49:55,680
‎We'll live in a new place
‎with new identities.

559
00:49:55,764 --> 00:49:56,765
‎We'll even have new names.

560
00:49:57,682 --> 00:49:58,517
‎I see.

561
00:50:01,770 --> 00:50:04,105
‎But I still want you to call me Min-ji.

562
00:50:04,189 --> 00:50:06,024
‎Why? You don't want to change your name?

563
00:50:06,107 --> 00:50:07,692
‎Mom gave me that name.

564
00:50:11,696 --> 00:50:12,864
‎Okay, I will.

565
00:50:14,074 --> 00:50:16,409
‎It feels like
‎we have our own little secret.

566
00:50:16,493 --> 00:50:17,327
‎Doesn't it?

567
00:50:21,122 --> 00:50:23,834
‎It won't be easy starting a new life.

568
00:50:24,459 --> 00:50:25,293
‎Will you be okay?

569
00:50:27,462 --> 00:50:28,880
‎I think it'll be fun.

570
00:50:30,882 --> 00:50:33,260
‎This life wasn't much fun anyway.

571
00:50:34,094 --> 00:50:35,512
‎I'll just consider this a new beginning.

572
00:50:40,725 --> 00:50:43,687
‎Then how about a new beginning
‎as a model student?

573
00:50:44,354 --> 00:50:46,147
‎You can study hard and go to college.

574
00:50:46,773 --> 00:50:47,858
‎What?

575
00:50:47,941 --> 00:50:49,442
‎Why do you get to decide that?

576
00:50:50,110 --> 00:50:52,404
‎You don't even know what I want to become.

577
00:50:52,487 --> 00:50:53,947
‎I can start learning now.

578
00:50:56,575 --> 00:50:58,285
‎What do you want to be, Min-ji?

579
00:51:00,161 --> 00:51:00,996
‎Me?

580
00:51:02,247 --> 00:51:03,123
‎Maybe a singer?

581
00:51:11,464 --> 00:51:12,382
‎What?

582
00:51:14,050 --> 00:51:15,886
‎If you take after me,
‎singing isn't your thing.

583
00:51:16,469 --> 00:51:18,388
‎What do you mean?

584
00:51:18,471 --> 00:51:20,348
‎I'm tone-deaf!

585
00:51:25,103 --> 00:51:25,937
‎Is that funny?

586
00:51:26,980 --> 00:51:28,315
‎My gosh.

587
00:51:32,485 --> 00:51:33,403
‎Mr. Kim.

588
00:51:34,905 --> 00:51:36,072
‎And Min-ji.

589
00:51:39,200 --> 00:51:40,660
‎Those are your new identities.

590
00:51:40,744 --> 00:51:43,246
‎There's a manual inside the file,
‎so learn it inside and out.

591
00:51:44,122 --> 00:51:45,290
‎Especially you, Min-ji.

592
00:51:54,883 --> 00:51:56,551
‎"Kim Ji-min"?

593
00:51:58,637 --> 00:52:00,388
‎You didn't even bother trying, did you?

594
00:52:00,472 --> 00:52:03,391
‎Well, coming up with new names
‎isn't our job.

595
00:52:06,311 --> 00:52:07,562
‎Thank you.

596
00:52:12,150 --> 00:52:14,527
‎I hope I never see your face again.

597
00:52:16,655 --> 00:52:17,739
‎Likewise.

598
00:52:18,698 --> 00:52:21,701
‎I don't really want to
‎see your face either.

599
00:52:21,785 --> 00:52:22,911
‎Me too.

600
00:52:22,994 --> 00:52:23,828
‎What?

601
00:52:26,539 --> 00:52:28,875
‎I've never seen you smile before, Mr. Kim.

602
00:52:29,542 --> 00:52:31,169
‎This is him cracking up.

603
00:52:31,252 --> 00:52:32,629
‎-Really?
‎-Yeah.

604
00:52:35,590 --> 00:52:36,591
‎Here.

605
00:52:38,176 --> 00:52:39,302
‎What is it?

606
00:52:40,929 --> 00:52:43,682
‎I hope you grow up to be
‎someone great and admirable.

607
00:52:50,355 --> 00:52:51,898
‎I guess it's kind of pretty.

608
00:52:52,524 --> 00:52:53,358
‎Thank you.

609
00:52:55,402 --> 00:52:57,612
‎He's much warmer than he seems.

610
00:52:59,114 --> 00:53:01,074
‎We chose that together.

611
00:53:01,157 --> 00:53:02,617
‎The three of you bought a single hairpin?

612
00:53:02,701 --> 00:53:03,702
‎It's an expensive one.

613
00:53:07,539 --> 00:53:09,082
‎-Do you like it?
‎-Yeah.

614
00:53:09,666 --> 00:53:11,209
‎-Get back to work.
‎-Right.

615
00:53:11,292 --> 00:53:12,377
‎-Yes, sir.
‎-Yes, sir.

616
00:53:22,303 --> 00:53:23,304
‎Mr. Kim!

617
00:53:24,222 --> 00:53:25,390
‎Kim!

618
00:53:27,976 --> 00:53:29,144
‎Take this.

619
00:53:30,103 --> 00:53:31,021
‎It's not much.

620
00:53:31,104 --> 00:53:32,605
‎It's to prevent bad luck.

621
00:53:33,356 --> 00:53:37,277
‎I thought a new suit would be fitting
‎for your fresh start.

622
00:53:37,902 --> 00:53:40,030
‎Wow, you're so lucky, Dad.

623
00:53:40,113 --> 00:53:42,615
‎Come on, take it. It's heavy.

624
00:53:42,699 --> 00:53:43,742
‎Thank you.

625
00:53:43,825 --> 00:53:47,454
‎Iron out the wrinkles in your suit,

626
00:53:47,537 --> 00:53:49,914
‎and the wrinkles in life
‎will iron themselves out.

627
00:53:51,833 --> 00:53:52,751
‎I'll remember that.

628
00:53:52,834 --> 00:53:56,546
‎Goodness, I wonder
‎when I'll get to see you again.

629
00:53:57,839 --> 00:53:58,882
‎By the way,

630
00:53:59,507 --> 00:54:02,093
‎we lived in the same neighborhood

631
00:54:02,177 --> 00:54:03,970
‎but never even knew each other's names.

632
00:54:05,263 --> 00:54:06,306
‎My name is

633
00:54:07,348 --> 00:54:08,808
‎Im Ho-won.

634
00:54:09,476 --> 00:54:10,477
‎My name is

635
00:54:11,811 --> 00:54:13,146
‎Kim…

636
00:54:14,355 --> 00:54:15,774
‎-Nice to meet you.
‎-Likewise.

637
00:54:16,399 --> 00:54:17,484
‎Please take care.

638
00:54:18,735 --> 00:54:19,819
‎-Take care.
‎-You too.

639
00:54:20,737 --> 00:54:21,571
‎Goodbye, then.

640
00:54:37,378 --> 00:54:39,714
‎ECOLOGICAL PARK

641
00:54:56,564 --> 00:54:57,899
‎-Min-ji.
‎-Yeah?

642
00:54:57,982 --> 00:54:59,275
‎Should we listen to some music?

643
00:55:05,365 --> 00:55:06,908
‎PLAYLIST FOR CHERRY BLOSSOM DAYS

644
00:55:25,969 --> 00:55:28,721
‎You know, people say you need new clothes
‎for a fresh start.

645
00:55:30,056 --> 00:55:32,183
‎Shouldn't I get
‎some new clothes too, then?

646
00:55:34,269 --> 00:55:36,312
‎Yeah, I should.

647
00:55:39,649 --> 00:55:40,817
‎I'm unemployed now.

648
00:55:42,652 --> 00:55:44,320
‎But you'll get a new job, right?

649
00:55:46,447 --> 00:55:47,282
‎Come on.

650
00:55:49,284 --> 00:55:50,368
‎All right.

651
00:55:50,451 --> 00:55:52,412
‎I'll buy you new clothes when I get a job.

652
00:55:52,996 --> 00:55:54,455
‎That's a promise, right?

653
00:55:54,539 --> 00:55:56,499
‎I'm going to ask for something
‎really expensive.

654
00:55:56,583 --> 00:55:57,500
‎All right.

655
00:56:22,817 --> 00:56:24,569
‎Your homeroom teacher is awful.

656
00:56:24,652 --> 00:56:27,989
‎How could he not even wish you good luck
‎when you're transferring?

657
00:56:28,072 --> 00:56:31,284
‎I heard things have been tense at school
‎because of Hye-ri.

658
00:56:31,367 --> 00:56:34,829
‎Yeah, I saw on social media that people
‎are calling it a school for criminals.

659
00:56:34,913 --> 00:56:36,206
‎I know.

660
00:56:49,802 --> 00:56:50,678
‎I guess

661
00:56:51,304 --> 00:56:53,056
‎you're really transferring.

662
00:56:54,140 --> 00:56:54,974
‎Yeah.

663
00:56:56,517 --> 00:56:57,518
‎I'm sorry.

664
00:56:58,269 --> 00:57:00,480
‎If only I hadn't messaged you that day…

665
00:57:04,400 --> 00:57:06,069
‎You didn't do it on purpose.

666
00:57:07,445 --> 00:57:08,279
‎It's okay.

667
00:57:10,406 --> 00:57:11,241
‎Then…

668
00:57:12,200 --> 00:57:13,284
‎Will you…

669
00:57:14,744 --> 00:57:16,287
‎message me after you transfer?

670
00:57:17,413 --> 00:57:18,373
‎I'll visit you.

671
00:57:22,544 --> 00:57:23,461
‎I don't think

672
00:57:24,629 --> 00:57:25,797
‎I can.

673
00:57:28,007 --> 00:57:28,883
‎Right.

674
00:57:29,676 --> 00:57:31,427
‎-I see.
‎-I'm sorry.

675
00:57:32,845 --> 00:57:34,556
‎No, don't be sorry.

676
00:57:40,853 --> 00:57:43,731
‎I think I should get going.

677
00:57:43,815 --> 00:57:44,816
‎Already?

678
00:57:44,899 --> 00:57:46,192
‎She's waiting for me.

679
00:57:48,653 --> 00:57:49,571
‎Take care.

680
00:58:05,920 --> 00:58:06,796
‎Here.

681
00:58:08,006 --> 00:58:11,718
‎KIM MIN-JI

682
00:58:11,801 --> 00:58:13,052
‎Will you…

683
00:58:14,178 --> 00:58:15,430
‎remember my name?

684
00:58:17,473 --> 00:58:18,308
‎Yeah.

685
00:58:19,183 --> 00:58:20,268
‎Kim Min-ji.

686
00:58:30,111 --> 00:58:31,112
‎How did it go?

687
00:58:33,990 --> 00:58:35,158
‎Let's go.

688
00:58:57,972 --> 00:58:59,015
‎This is it. What do you think?

689
00:58:59,098 --> 00:59:00,808
‎Oh my gosh, it's so pretty!

690
00:59:00,892 --> 00:59:02,268
‎-Come on, let's go.
‎-All right.

691
00:59:07,899 --> 00:59:09,442
‎Hey, Kim!

692
00:59:10,526 --> 00:59:12,362
‎Uncle?

693
00:59:13,988 --> 00:59:14,906
‎-Hey.
‎-Hey.

694
00:59:17,158 --> 00:59:18,785
‎Hey, what a great house.

695
00:59:19,535 --> 00:59:20,620
‎Is it a rental or did you buy it?

696
00:59:21,204 --> 00:59:23,247
‎Min-ji, did you do well on your exams?

697
00:59:23,331 --> 00:59:24,582
‎Of course.

698
00:59:24,666 --> 00:59:25,500
‎She's a level eight.

699
00:59:25,583 --> 00:59:26,918
‎Wow, level eight?

700
00:59:27,001 --> 00:59:28,628
‎-I'm jealous.
‎-What about Da-bin?

701
00:59:29,212 --> 00:59:31,130
‎-She's healthy.
‎-That's all that matters.

702
00:59:31,214 --> 00:59:32,048
‎Hey, Kim.

703
00:59:37,637 --> 00:59:39,972
‎Hey, why are there so many boxes?

704
00:59:40,056 --> 00:59:41,182
‎Do we have to move all of this?

705
00:59:41,265 --> 00:59:42,141
‎Oh my.

706
00:59:42,850 --> 00:59:44,018
‎Hey.

707
00:59:44,602 --> 00:59:46,354
‎So you ‎do‎ own other clothes.

708
00:59:47,689 --> 00:59:48,731
‎You look great.

709
00:59:50,149 --> 00:59:52,360
‎I told you I have a lot of clothes.

710
00:59:53,361 --> 00:59:55,029
‎-You look really rich.
‎-Do I?

711
00:59:56,322 --> 00:59:58,282
‎Hey, hold on.

712
00:59:58,366 --> 00:59:59,951
‎We're moving boxes,
‎and you came dressed like that?

713
01:00:00,034 --> 01:00:00,952
‎Yeah.

714
01:00:01,035 --> 01:00:02,245
‎Why?

715
01:00:02,328 --> 01:00:04,747
‎Well, you know, it's a special day.

716
01:00:05,915 --> 01:00:06,999
‎Have you lost your mind?

717
01:00:07,083 --> 01:00:08,668
‎Be honest. You wore this
‎to avoid working, didn't you?

718
01:00:08,751 --> 01:00:10,962
‎I'm tired. Stop talking to me.

719
01:00:11,045 --> 01:00:11,963
‎You're tired?

720
01:00:12,046 --> 01:00:15,633
‎Eat one of these, get an energy boost,
‎and start moving boxes.

721
01:00:17,927 --> 01:00:21,723
‎And one for each of you
‎before you get to work.

722
01:00:22,890 --> 01:00:23,850
‎Here.

723
01:00:24,392 --> 01:00:25,518
‎And one for me too.

724
01:00:27,979 --> 01:00:29,731
‎This tastes just like coffee.

725
01:00:30,648 --> 01:00:31,482
‎It's good.

726
01:00:31,983 --> 01:00:34,610
‎Just how many of those
‎do you have at home?

727
01:00:34,694 --> 01:00:36,070
‎-Do you want a box?
‎-I sure do.

728
01:00:36,154 --> 01:00:37,363
‎Are you moving in or not?

729
01:00:37,447 --> 01:00:38,364
‎Coming!

730
01:00:38,448 --> 01:00:40,241
‎Hey, let's finish up quickly and go eat.

731
01:00:40,324 --> 01:00:42,660
‎-Hurry up and unload.
‎-Get a move on!

732
01:00:42,744 --> 01:00:43,953
‎-Here we go.
‎-Let's go.

733
01:00:44,036 --> 01:00:45,997
‎-Move some boxes, punk.
‎-Okay.

734
01:00:46,080 --> 01:00:47,373
‎-All right.
‎-Let's go.

735
01:00:47,457 --> 01:00:48,750
‎-Quickly, quickly.
‎-What are you doing?

736
01:00:48,833 --> 01:00:50,543
‎-Hurry up now.
‎-Hurry up!

737
01:00:50,626 --> 01:00:52,920
‎All right, here we go.

738
01:00:58,009 --> 01:00:59,886
‎-That's the last one, right?
‎-Yeah.

739
01:01:00,470 --> 01:01:01,888
‎Yeah, you little weasel.

740
01:01:01,971 --> 01:01:03,765
‎You didn't even lift a finger.

741
01:01:03,848 --> 01:01:05,600
‎All you did was carry the light boxes.

742
01:01:05,683 --> 01:01:07,769
‎How can you look Min-ji in the eye?

743
01:01:07,852 --> 01:01:10,188
‎Hey, Kim Min-ji-min… Ji-min.
‎Why are you laughing?

744
01:01:10,271 --> 01:01:13,816
‎Do you want to see me get hurt
‎while carrying heavy boxes?

745
01:01:13,900 --> 01:01:15,902
‎No, of course not.

746
01:01:16,652 --> 01:01:18,196
‎Let's go eat. I'll take care of the rest.

747
01:01:18,279 --> 01:01:20,281
‎Why bother? Let's just order ‎jjajangmyeon‎.

748
01:01:20,865 --> 01:01:22,366
‎-‎Jjajangmyeon‎ is the best on moving days.
‎-Hey.

749
01:01:23,034 --> 01:01:24,535
‎Why do you get to choose the menu?

750
01:01:24,619 --> 01:01:26,287
‎Eat whatever Min-ji wants to have.

751
01:01:26,370 --> 01:01:27,830
‎What do you want, Min-ji? You decide.

752
01:01:28,414 --> 01:01:30,625
‎-Jjajangmyeon sounds good to--
‎-Did you say sushi? Okay.

753
01:01:30,708 --> 01:01:31,793
‎Sushi sounds great.

754
01:01:32,460 --> 01:01:34,295
‎Your daughter wants sushi.

755
01:01:37,131 --> 01:01:38,966
‎You must really like sushi.

756
01:01:40,885 --> 01:01:43,387
‎-Yeah, I love it.
‎-See?

757
01:01:43,471 --> 01:01:45,139
‎Let's go have sushi.

758
01:01:45,932 --> 01:01:47,099
‎-Get changed first.
‎-Let's go change.

759
01:01:47,183 --> 01:01:49,602
‎-Han-soo, you're really something else.
‎-Okay.

760
01:01:51,521 --> 01:01:53,815
‎You know, come to think of it,
‎you always wear the same outfit.

761
01:01:55,817 --> 01:01:56,692
‎What are you looking at?

762
01:01:59,779 --> 01:02:01,948
‎Darn it, I can't see without my glasses.

763
01:02:02,698 --> 01:02:04,659
‎Hey, I want to see.

764
01:02:04,742 --> 01:02:06,911
‎-Let me take a look.
‎-You can just look at that.

765
01:02:06,994 --> 01:02:07,829
‎Oh, it's all here.

766
01:02:07,912 --> 01:02:09,956
‎-Thank you.
‎-Gosh, there are so many items.

767
01:02:10,039 --> 01:02:13,125
‎My stomach will be full of fish
‎swimming around.

768
01:02:13,209 --> 01:02:16,087
‎Hey, Kim Min-ji-min.
‎You made a spectacular choice.

769
01:02:16,170 --> 01:02:17,505
‎Order whatever you want.

770
01:02:17,588 --> 01:02:19,590
‎-What are you having?
‎-I think I'll have--

771
01:02:19,674 --> 01:02:22,176
‎Can we get one flounder…
‎Actually, make it five. What else?

772
01:02:22,802 --> 01:02:24,011
‎Don't be shy.

773
01:02:24,762 --> 01:02:27,098
‎And can we get five plates
‎of yellowfin tuna belly?

774
01:02:27,765 --> 01:02:29,475
‎Here, have salmon. You like it, right?

775
01:02:30,685 --> 01:02:31,894
‎You like it too.

776
01:02:32,395 --> 01:02:34,146
‎One more salmon, please.

777
01:02:34,230 --> 01:02:36,232
‎Make it five, please.
‎Do you want some too?

778
01:02:36,315 --> 01:02:37,900
‎-Of course.
‎-Actually, make it ten.

779
01:02:44,532 --> 01:02:46,325
‎Why are you eating with your hands?

780
01:02:46,951 --> 01:02:48,119
‎That's how you eat sushi.

781
01:02:52,456 --> 01:02:54,000
‎There's no eel here, what a shame.

782
01:02:59,422 --> 01:03:00,548
‎Is it good?

783
01:03:00,631 --> 01:03:02,633
‎Yeah, it's dangerously good.

784
01:03:02,717 --> 01:03:04,510
‎He wasn't asking you, Uncle.

785
01:03:04,594 --> 01:03:05,428
‎Sorry.

786
01:03:06,053 --> 01:03:07,054
‎It's good.

787
01:03:07,138 --> 01:03:07,972
‎Eat up.

788
01:03:08,055 --> 01:03:08,973
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

789
01:03:10,099 --> 01:03:11,100
‎Eat up, you guys.

790
01:03:11,183 --> 01:03:12,018
‎Okay.

791
01:03:12,810 --> 01:03:15,813
‎-Sir, you forgot the monkfish liver.
‎-What else do you want?

792
01:03:18,649 --> 01:03:21,402
‎A new neighborhood, a new school…

793
01:03:25,031 --> 01:03:27,366
‎and a new name I don't like.

794
01:03:31,829 --> 01:03:33,748
‎Min-ji, come have breakfast!

795
01:03:34,916 --> 01:03:36,000
‎Kim Min-ji!

796
01:03:37,793 --> 01:03:38,836
‎I'm late.

797
01:03:38,920 --> 01:03:40,922
‎A lot of things have changed,

798
01:03:41,005 --> 01:03:43,591
‎but my dad and I haven't ‎changed
‎all ‎that ‎much.

799
01:03:48,054 --> 01:03:50,514
‎I'll eat after I get back. Save me some.

800
01:03:52,308 --> 01:03:53,309
‎Okay, I will.

801
01:03:53,935 --> 01:03:54,977
‎Be safe.

802
01:03:55,978 --> 01:03:57,229
‎And don't get into any fights!

803
01:03:57,855 --> 01:03:59,273
‎I won't!

804
01:03:59,357 --> 01:04:02,109
‎Except for my dad laughing more often now.

805
01:04:03,110 --> 01:04:04,195
‎Hello, ma'am.

806
01:04:04,278 --> 01:04:06,197
‎Pure hearts, pure manners.
‎Join Pure Taekwondo.

807
01:04:06,280 --> 01:04:09,909
‎-And my uncles are still the same.
‎-We're offering free trial classes.

808
01:04:09,992 --> 01:04:10,826
‎Thank you.

809
01:04:10,910 --> 01:04:11,994
‎Hello.

810
01:04:12,078 --> 01:04:15,081
‎-Look who's back.
‎-We're offering free trial classes.

811
01:04:15,164 --> 01:04:16,999
‎-Who's that man over there?
‎-It's not on the flyer,

812
01:04:17,083 --> 01:04:20,461
‎but we play dodgeball,
‎and there are prizes, so come by, okay?

813
01:04:20,544 --> 01:04:21,629
‎-Hello, ma'am.
‎-Cross slowly!

814
01:04:21,712 --> 01:04:23,339
‎Please cross the street now.

815
01:04:23,422 --> 01:04:25,508
‎Pure Taekwondo
‎is located on the third floor.

816
01:04:25,591 --> 01:04:27,760
‎Feel free to drop by
‎during the free trial period.

817
01:04:27,843 --> 01:04:29,553
‎Hello, ma'am.

818
01:04:30,137 --> 01:04:31,389
‎Should we stop him?

819
01:04:31,973 --> 01:04:33,975
‎Leave him be. It's a nice sight.

820
01:04:34,058 --> 01:04:35,226
‎I bet he was a big club-goer.

821
01:04:35,309 --> 01:04:38,604
‎POLICE

822
01:04:42,692 --> 01:04:44,860
‎The weather is so nice.

823
01:04:45,611 --> 01:04:47,071
‎I know, right?

824
01:04:47,154 --> 01:04:48,864
‎It was really cold not too long ago.

825
01:04:48,948 --> 01:04:50,783
‎-Please enjoy.
‎-Thank you.

826
01:04:51,450 --> 01:04:52,451
‎Let's eat.

827
01:04:52,535 --> 01:04:53,577
‎This looks good.

828
01:04:53,661 --> 01:04:55,037
‎Hold on. We need to take a photo.

829
01:04:56,288 --> 01:04:58,749
‎Sang-a hangs out with me sometimes.

830
01:05:04,797 --> 01:05:05,673
‎Sang-a.

831
01:05:07,299 --> 01:05:09,260
‎You're here to keep an eye on me, right?

832
01:05:09,343 --> 01:05:10,970
‎No, I'm not.

833
01:05:11,053 --> 01:05:12,763
‎You think you're special?

834
01:05:12,847 --> 01:05:14,098
‎No.

835
01:05:14,181 --> 01:05:15,433
‎Who saved your life?

836
01:05:15,516 --> 01:05:16,350
‎You did.

837
01:05:16,434 --> 01:05:17,810
‎Then who should you be thanking?

838
01:05:17,893 --> 01:05:18,853
‎You?

839
01:05:18,936 --> 01:05:19,812
‎So who should pay for this?

840
01:05:20,980 --> 01:05:22,148
‎You?

841
01:05:24,483 --> 01:05:25,860
‎Right, I should pay.

842
01:05:25,943 --> 01:05:26,861
‎Dig in.

843
01:05:26,944 --> 01:05:28,821
‎Thank you.

844
01:05:30,322 --> 01:05:32,116
‎How are things with your dad?

845
01:05:32,199 --> 01:05:33,534
‎Is he more affectionate than before?

846
01:05:35,244 --> 01:05:37,413
‎No, he's still the same.

847
01:05:37,496 --> 01:05:38,330
‎Right.

848
01:05:38,414 --> 01:05:40,541
‎That's not really who he is, is it?

849
01:05:40,624 --> 01:05:41,917
‎It's totally not him.

850
01:05:42,418 --> 01:05:44,211
‎Any good news lately, Sang-a?

851
01:05:45,129 --> 01:05:49,133
‎-He was like, "You can't date yet."
‎-Really?

852
01:05:50,051 --> 01:05:51,260
‎I'm not surprised.

853
01:05:58,893 --> 01:06:01,020
‎Allow me to present today's special.

854
01:06:03,522 --> 01:06:05,691
‎These would be good for when I do this.

855
01:06:09,236 --> 01:06:11,322
‎Do you have regular glasses
‎instead of sunglasses?

856
01:06:12,782 --> 01:06:13,699
‎Who are you?

857
01:06:15,951 --> 01:06:17,828
‎I usually don't show this to anyone,
‎but here goes.

858
01:06:18,412 --> 01:06:20,206
‎"Brother Monkey, what's gotten into you?"

859
01:06:21,082 --> 01:06:22,666
‎Hello.

860
01:06:22,750 --> 01:06:24,543
‎My name is Kim. Nice to meet you.

861
01:06:26,879 --> 01:06:29,548
‎In my opinion, this case is…

862
01:06:30,549 --> 01:06:32,051
‎Rock and roll.

863
01:06:38,474 --> 01:06:39,642
‎Hey, Han-soo, Jin-cheol.

864
01:06:40,226 --> 01:06:41,393
‎You think Min-ji will approve?

865
01:06:42,686 --> 01:06:43,687
‎Probably not.

866
01:06:43,771 --> 01:06:46,649
‎Hey, what do you think?
‎They suit me, right?

867
01:06:46,732 --> 01:06:47,650
‎-You look weird.
‎-You look weird.

868
01:06:47,733 --> 01:06:48,609
‎Damn it.

869
01:06:49,110 --> 01:06:51,153
‎Just kidding.
‎You look like Tony Leung Chiu-wai.

870
01:06:51,237 --> 01:06:54,156
‎Tony Leung Chiu-wai, my foot.
‎He looks like a brewery owner.

871
01:06:54,240 --> 01:06:57,660
‎Hey, you look like a middle-aged man
‎desperate to look young.

872
01:06:57,743 --> 01:06:58,828
‎That's what we are.

873
01:07:00,079 --> 01:07:01,080
‎Right.

874
01:07:01,956 --> 01:07:02,873
‎We're middle-aged men.

875
01:07:03,457 --> 01:07:04,542
‎Middle-aged men with glasses.

876
01:07:06,710 --> 01:07:09,255
‎Now that I'm wearing glasses again
‎after a while,

877
01:07:09,880 --> 01:07:11,674
‎I feel like
‎they're weighing my shoulders down.

878
01:07:11,757 --> 01:07:12,883
‎Should we take them off?

879
01:07:12,967 --> 01:07:16,262
‎No. It's better to be
‎middle-aged men with glasses.

880
01:07:17,388 --> 01:07:18,305
‎-Let's go.
‎-Okay.

881
01:07:19,181 --> 01:07:20,933
‎-Goodbye, sir.
‎-Oh, goodbye.

882
01:07:21,016 --> 01:07:21,934
‎-Thank you.
‎-Goodbye.

883
01:07:22,017 --> 01:07:23,686
‎-Have a good day.
‎-Take care.

884
01:07:23,769 --> 01:07:26,772
‎-There wasn't much to choose from.
‎-You tried on 145 pairs.

885
01:07:33,863 --> 01:07:36,574
‎It feels pretty good
‎to wear new glasses though.

886
01:07:36,657 --> 01:07:39,034
‎Yeah, I feel like I could fly!

887
01:07:40,119 --> 01:07:41,203
‎Hey, mister.

888
01:07:41,996 --> 01:07:44,498
‎You should never mess with
‎middle-aged men with glasses.

889
01:07:44,582 --> 01:07:47,001
‎-Yeah, someone could get someone hurt.
‎-Who?

890
01:07:47,084 --> 01:07:49,712
‎The one who messed with them
‎or the middle-aged men with glasses?

891
01:07:50,337 --> 01:07:51,213
‎I'm not sure.

892
01:07:52,590 --> 01:07:55,718
‎All dads in the world
‎are just regular people.

893
01:07:56,302 --> 01:07:58,053
‎-They work to support their families,
‎-What's with the color?

894
01:07:58,137 --> 01:08:00,014
‎-and they're afraid of moms.
‎-Guys, check it out.

895
01:08:00,097 --> 01:08:01,849
‎-And sometimes after work‎…
‎-Did you ask for these?

896
01:08:01,932 --> 01:08:03,142
‎They're transition lenses.

897
01:08:03,225 --> 01:08:05,144
‎-…‎they come home with smelly feet.
‎-I didn't ask for these though.

898
01:08:05,227 --> 01:08:06,312
‎They give off a middle-aged man vibe.

899
01:08:06,395 --> 01:08:07,396
‎Man, these are slick.

900
01:08:07,479 --> 01:08:11,901
‎It may be hard to believe, but my dad
‎is also just a regular middle-aged man.

901
01:08:14,945 --> 01:08:15,779
‎Well,

902
01:08:16,405 --> 01:08:18,324
‎as long as no one messes with me.

903
01:08:22,369 --> 01:08:28,000
‎HAPPINESS ROAD, HAENGBOK-RO

904
01:08:38,219 --> 01:08:43,140
‎BAEKHO LABOR AGENCY

905
01:08:45,976 --> 01:08:46,894
‎Oh, I almost forgot.

906
01:08:47,478 --> 01:08:49,271
‎I think my dad's getting a new job.

907
01:08:50,814 --> 01:08:53,525
‎Someone he knew back in the day
‎introduced him to it.

908
01:09:00,074 --> 01:09:01,951
‎Juhak Construction is nothing.

909
01:09:02,034 --> 01:09:05,204
‎I'll chop it up like a cucumber

910
01:09:05,287 --> 01:09:07,665
‎and make a salad out of it.

911
01:09:08,249 --> 01:09:10,209
‎You know this will cost you, right?

912
01:09:13,587 --> 01:09:14,922
‎3RD FLOOR

913
01:09:34,692 --> 01:09:35,734
‎May I help you?

914
01:09:41,365 --> 01:09:42,199
‎Excuse me.

915
01:09:42,992 --> 01:09:44,285
‎I'm here for an interview--

916
01:09:44,368 --> 01:09:45,619
‎Check and check!

917
01:09:45,703 --> 01:09:48,414
‎I just checked your résumé, Kim!

918
01:09:49,290 --> 01:09:50,874
‎But you know,

919
01:09:51,458 --> 01:09:55,796
‎I'm not sure if I can trust this.

920
01:09:59,133 --> 01:10:00,384
‎Now then.

921
01:10:00,467 --> 01:10:02,261
‎Shall we start

922
01:10:02,344 --> 01:10:03,887
‎the interview?

923
01:10:47,473 --> 01:10:50,392
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

924
01:10:54,480 --> 01:11:00,402
‎STAY TUNED FOR A BONUS SCENE

925
01:11:30,766 --> 01:11:34,478
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

926
01:11:34,561 --> 01:11:36,146
‎BONUS SCENE

927
01:11:36,230 --> 01:11:40,192
‎IN 2006, THERE WAS A FAMOUS TRIO
‎IN THE CHEONSAN UNIT

928
01:11:43,737 --> 01:11:44,696
‎CHEONSAN

929
01:12:00,462 --> 01:12:02,047
‎Korea's iron teeth!

930
01:12:02,840 --> 01:12:04,299
‎They're unbreakable!

931
01:12:06,051 --> 01:12:07,636
‎Korea's iron teeth!

932
01:12:39,501 --> 01:12:42,546
‎PARK JIN-CHEOL

933
01:12:42,629 --> 01:12:44,423
‎YOON KYUNG-HO

934
01:12:44,506 --> 01:12:47,468
‎SUNG HAN-SOO

935
01:12:47,551 --> 01:12:49,428
‎CHOI DAE-HOON

936
01:12:49,511 --> 01:12:52,639
‎KIM

937
01:12:52,723 --> 01:12:57,644
‎SO JI-SUB

938
01:12:57,728 --> 01:12:59,354
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

939
